index=* EventCode=4624
| search Authentication_Package=NTLM
| table _time Account_Name Logon_Type Authentication_Package Source_Network_Address Workstation_Name
| sort - _time


This closely matches what you actually documented.

Your report says the PtH investigation focused on Windows Event ID 4624, then filtered successful logons for NTLM/network authentication characteristics, and correlated the events with the Kali attacker source.

Again, we're not saying:

NTLM = Pass-the-Hash

because normal NTLM authentication can occur legitimately.

Instead, it helps identify authentication that becomes suspicious when you have:

Privileged account
        +
NTLM
        +
Unexpected source
        +
Network logon
